{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Sends a conversation and optional tool definitions to the configured LLM and returns {kind: text|tool_calls|error, content|tool_calls, assistant_message}. THE provider engine's thin GATE: LLM= in runtime/agent/botd.properties picks an arm, this resolves it (applying <ARM>_HEADERS and the <ARM>_KEY/<ARM>_API_KEY auth) and delegates to the per-provider command under agent.llm - llm_openai (VLLM/OPENAI and OpenAI-compatible endpoints), llm_anthropic (native /v1/messages), llm_gemini (native generateContent), llm_ollama (native /api/chat), llm_local (resident model service), llm_remote (a peer running its own chat_llm), or LLM_CTL=lib:ctl:cmd for anything custom. Every dialect normalizes into the same OpenAI-shaped result, and the LLM_CAPTURE seam wraps the whole dispatch here, so capture and the result contract live in exactly one place. VISION: a message may carry an `images` array of image file paths; each dialect renders them in its own envelope. Retries only 408/429/5xx/transport. ask_llm and tool_loop call this command.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::command::Command;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\n\nuse crate::agent::msg::put::put;\nuse crate::agent::llm::llm_common::*;","params":[{"name":"messages","type":"JSONArray"},{"name":"tools","type":"JSONArray"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"ytohmk19f70b2c09ck7ce2","readers":[],"time":1790869005494,"username":"system","writers":[]}